    "text": "To determine Jessica's guess for the total number of red and white jelly beans in the fishbowl, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total number of jelly beans in one bag:**\n   - Red: 24\n   - Black: 13\n   - Green: 36\n   - Purple: 28\n   - Yellow: 32\n   - White: 18\n\n   Adding these together:\n   \\[\n   24 + 13 + 36 + 28 + 32 + 18 = 167\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the number of bags needed to fill the fishbowl:**\n   Jessica assumed it would take three bags to fill the fishbowl.\n\n3. **Calculate the total number of jelly beans in the fishbowl:**\n   \\[\n   167 \\text{ jelly beans/bag} \\times 3 \\text{ bags} = 501 \\text{ jelly beans}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Identify the number of red and white jelly beans in one bag:**\n   - Red: 24\n   - White: 18\n\n5. **Calculate the total number of red and white jelly beans in one bag:**\n   \\[\n   24 \\text{ red} + 18 \\text{ white} = 42 \\text{ red and white jelly beans}\n   \\]\n\n6. **Determine the total number of red and white jelly beans in the fishbowl:**\n   Since Jessica bought one bag, her guess for the total number of red and white jelly beans in the fishbowl is the same as the number of red and white jelly beans in one bag.\n\nTherefore, Jessica's guess is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{42}\n\\]",
